# Git's default hunk-header pattern matches any line starting in column one,
# which inside a long class reports every method as the class. `Splitting a
# file` in docs/decisions.md decides where a file's seams are by reading those
# headers -- two definitions belong together when a commit touched both -- and
# without this it sees a long module as one definition touched 232 times.
#
# That entry says so, and the setting it describes lived in `core.attributesFile`
# on one machine, pointing into a temporary directory that no longer exists. A
# measurement nobody else can run is a measurement that stops being checked.
*.py diff=python
